# Suite stic: the STIC register file, the access windows, the display-enable handshake and the frame timeline (VID-01, plan 06-06).
# Plan 06-06 task 2: the timeline family (stic.events.*, stic.reset.*, stic.slice.*); later tasks of the plan add the access, register,
# hook, profile and judge families.
# Plan 06-06 task 3: the access family (stic.alias.*, stic.window.*, stic.blocked.*, stic.enable.seq.*, stic.mode.*): the write and read aliases, the windows, the blocked policy and its counters, the display-enable handshake and the mode select, from stand-in guests and synthesized accesses through the bus wrapper.
# Plan 06-06 task 4: the literal-probe families (stic.table.*, stic.reg.*, stic.hook.*, stic.profile.*, stic.judge.*): the register file and the hook classes judged against the independent register, memory-map and geometry literals, the window edges as profile perturbations, and three judge self-controls.
